1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,443
Tradeflow is a review tool
for the Dhaka Stock Exchange.

2
00:00:03,443 --> 00:00:08,239
It explains why the portfolio moved,
checks the reason behind every trade, and

3
00:00:08,239 --> 00:00:10,390
reviews a trade before you save it.

4
00:00:10,390 --> 00:00:15,124
Every number in every answer cites the
query that produced it, and a separate

5
00:00:15,124 --> 00:00:18,321
Evaluator rejects any claim
the rows cannot support.

6
00:00:18,321 --> 00:00:19,920
All the data is synthetic.

7
00:00:20,433 --> 00:00:22,463
This is the portfolio dashboard.

8
00:00:22,463 --> 00:00:27,730
At the top: market value, this week's move
against the DSEX index, dividend income,

9
00:00:27,730 --> 00:00:30,521
and realised and unrealised
profit and loss.

10
00:00:30,521 --> 00:00:35,661
Scrolling down shows what moved the
portfolio this week, each stock compared with

11
00:00:35,661 --> 00:00:38,960
its sector index, and the
contribution to the total.

12
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:44,163
Then the rules your portfolio breaks, and
the full holdings table with weights and

13
00:00:44,163 --> 00:00:45,305
break-even prices.

14
00:00:45,305 --> 00:00:48,033
The review agents live
on the Explain page.

15
00:00:48,533 --> 00:00:49,954
This is the Explain page.

16
00:00:49,954 --> 00:00:53,420
Pick a question, or type your
own, and press Explain my week.

17
00:00:53,420 --> 00:00:58,194
Watch each step appear live: the Planner
chooses the queries, code runs them against

18
00:00:58,194 --> 00:01:02,797
Zetaris or the local ledger, the Analyst
writes findings where every number cites

19
00:01:02,797 --> 00:01:07,570
the query behind it, the Evaluator checks
each claim against the rows and scores the

20
00:01:07,570 --> 00:01:10,980
draft out of nine, and the Writer
produces the final review.

21
00:01:10,980 --> 00:01:15,355
The Proof cards count the sponsor work:
queries run through Zetaris, memories

22
00:01:15,355 --> 00:01:20,072
recalled by the H-MEM engine, Nemotron
model calls with their token counts, and the

23
00:01:20,072 --> 00:01:21,834
guards that checked or blocked.

24
00:01:21,834 --> 00:01:26,209
Click a citation tag to open the exact
rows behind a number, and the SQL that

25
00:01:26,209 --> 00:01:27,009
Zetaris ran.

26
00:01:27,009 --> 00:01:31,385
At the bottom, the Correct this box lets
you teach the next review what to do

27
00:01:31,385 --> 00:01:32,185
differently.

28
00:01:32,433 --> 00:01:35,853
The agents never recommend
buying, selling or holding.

29
00:01:35,853 --> 00:01:39,019
These red chips are the
try-to-break-it questions.

30
00:01:39,019 --> 00:01:43,896
Click the advice question and the run
refuses to advise, marked by the advice

31
00:01:43,896 --> 00:01:46,683
declined badge, but
still reviews the facts.

32
00:01:46,683 --> 00:01:50,419
And an off-topic request, like
a poem, is kept to the data.

33
00:01:50,419 --> 00:01:53,649
The guards check every
reply before it reaches you.

34
00:01:54,133 --> 00:01:58,999
The Theses tab checks every trade reason
from your journal against the latest market

35
00:01:58,999 --> 00:01:59,799
data.

36
00:01:59,799 --> 00:02:04,549
For each entry it reads the thesis, the
exit condition and the horizon, then pulls

37
00:02:04,549 --> 00:02:08,141
the fundamentals, dividends and
announcements for that symbol.

38
00:02:08,141 --> 00:02:12,543
Each thesis gets a clear verdict:
confirmed, contradicted, or open, with the

39
00:02:12,543 --> 00:02:13,992
evidence that settles it.

40
00:02:13,992 --> 00:02:18,858
The table shows at a glance which of your
reasons still hold and which need a second

41
00:02:18,858 --> 00:02:19,658
look.

42
00:02:19,133 --> 00:02:22,269
Before you save a trade,
run the pre-trade check.

43
00:02:22,269 --> 00:02:27,325
Enter a symbol, choose buy or sell, and
set the quantity — here, buying seventy

44
00:02:27,325 --> 00:02:28,413
WALTONHIL shares.

45
00:02:28,413 --> 00:02:33,085
The agents run a what-if preview
against your open theses and your rules.

46
00:02:33,085 --> 00:02:38,397
This trade pushes a sector past its target,
so a clear warning appears: Nothing has

47
00:02:38,397 --> 00:02:40,573
been saved, the decision is yours.

48
00:02:40,573 --> 00:02:42,941
The check never writes to the ledger.

49
00:02:43,433 --> 00:02:47,995
The Reconcile tab compares the broker
and bank statements against the ledger.

50
00:02:47,995 --> 00:02:52,320
The code joins the sources on the
trading day, symbol, side and quantity.

51
00:02:52,320 --> 00:02:57,178
Each difference the agents explain, and
each one carries a proposed fix written by

52
00:02:57,178 --> 00:02:58,541
code, never by a model.

53
00:02:58,541 --> 00:03:03,281
You approve one at a time, and only your
approval applies the fix to the ledger.

54
00:03:03,767 --> 00:03:08,709
The review queue lists every run that
needs you: escalated trades, reconciliation

55
00:03:08,709 --> 00:03:10,967
proposals, and runs that hit a limit.

56
00:03:10,967 --> 00:03:15,055
All decisions are yours, and nothing
happens without your approval.

57
00:03:15,055 --> 00:03:19,815
Open a trace to see the whole run as a
timeline: every agent step, every guard

58
00:03:19,815 --> 00:03:24,818
decision, every retry and fallback, and
every model call with its tokens and cost.

59
00:03:24,818 --> 00:03:27,503
This is the audit trail
behind every answer.

60
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:29,864
Tradeflow review agents.

61
00:03:29,864 --> 00:03:32,039
Every claim cites its query.

62
00:03:32,039 --> 00:03:35,301
Every number is verified against the rows.

63
00:03:35,301 --> 00:03:36,699
You always decide.

64
00:03:36,699 --> 00:03:43,067
Built with NVIDIA Nemotron through Meterless
Nightshift and Zetaris Lightning SQL.

65
00:03:43,067 --> 00:03:44,776
All data is synthetic.
